From: Carl Andersson <carl.andersson@dynamist.se>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/fs: never announce submounts

A guest that receives FUSE_ATTR_SUBMOUNT makes the submount an automount
dentry, and overlayfs refuses one as a lower layer: ovl_dentry_weird
rejects DCACHE_NEED_AUTOMOUNT, and every lookup below it fails with
EREMOTE.

vivarium shares the host's /nix, where /nix/store is a bind of itself,
and the guest mounts an overlay over it as its own /nix. Announced, the
NixOS initrd fails at "Find NixOS closure".

virtiofsd has --no-announce-submounts for this. libkrun has no switch,
so this turns the announcement off. The cost is the same as virtiofsd's:
the guest sees one inode number space across the host filesystems below
the share.
---
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/linux/passthrough.rs	2026-10-24 17:53:41.118013000 +0200
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/linux/passthrough.rs	2026-10-24 17:53:51.190121575 +0200
@@ -914,10 +914,10 @@
             self.writeback.store(true, Ordering::Relaxed);
         }
 
-        if capable.contains(FsOptions::SUBMOUNTS) {
-            opts |= FsOptions::SUBMOUNTS;
-            self.announce_submounts.store(true, Ordering::Relaxed);
-        }
+        // Submounts are never announced, as virtiofsd's
+        // --no-announce-submounts: overlayfs refuses an automount dentry
+        // as a lower layer, so a share with a submount below it could not
+        // be one.
 
         Ok(opts)
     }
